From 87d42a94bde8923a373c86ab661176fbd54bb904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:14:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] port the Vulkan platform to metal2vulkan
 development 0db5825a

Builds on metal2vulkan 0db5825a with patches/metal2vulkan applied:
upstream development 0db5825a, the env-gated Arrow Lake-S facts
(M2V_ARL_FACTS, c7c4784c) and PixelFormatInfo::of / TextureLevelInfo::of
(0d31d29c, the release's format table without a device). Cargo.toml's
[patch] points there; Cargo.lock is unchanged.

One release, no Metal level. Upstream ec72c052 answers as macOS 27.0.1 on
every host and removed rt::MetalLevel, DeviceOptions::metal_level and
DeviceProperties::metal_level. Removed with them: os::METAL_LEVEL,
platform's metal_level, answering_level, answered_at and BELOW_HOST,
TextureFields::made_at_level, format_info's level_decides,
describes_answer and level helpers, and this crate's Inexact::MetalLevel
(inexact-metal-level), which nothing can relay any more. Guest-visible
answers on Linux are unchanged: this platform already named
MacOS27_0_1 there, and the runtime's single table is that release's.
Pixel format descriptions, the 264 described formats, which values
setPixelFormat: takes (every value the runtime names, the 13
three-channel formats included), a view's nil, level layouts, private
properties and a depth/stencil state's gpuResourceID (0) are as before.
Only a macOS host changes: its own release no longer picks 26.7.

format_info reads the table through PixelFormatInfo::of where it holds
no device (described, name, block) and through the device where it has
one (description, level_layout), as before. setter_takes is "the
runtime has a format of the value", which is what 27.0.1's row answered.
The functions keep their sel argument, unused now, so the callers
(macOS-only tests among them) are unchanged.

REIMS_VGPU_EXACT keeps the two policies the runtime still has,
batch_order and host_page_textures. The other 14 names (sampling,
ycbcr_filter, float_maths, texel_conversion, vertex_normalized,
half_rounding, nan_and_min_max, rounding_order, half_blend,
half_texel_bits, multisample_depth_twin, decoded_texels, tile_store,
resolve) are dropped from the match and EXACT_FORMS: upstream's "native
arithmetic" round (4817f3bd, 79166a74, 7e869009, 9afdb1e1, e87d6e55,
78ed264c, b7a62be6) removed those policies with no replacement, so a
name of one is now "ignored" on stderr. "all" is still the runtime's
exact_answers(), which today also sets half_chains to EachOperation
(only matters on a device without shaderFloat16). Every device still
takes CompletionPolicy::Exact and HeapCompressionPolicy::Uncompressed.

Removed degradation kinds. Dropped from DIES: UnormDepthSlope (70068f7c),
BeyondMeasuredDeviation (d4412c9c), DeviceGatherFootprint,
CubeFaceReciprocal, DeviceDepthComparison, DeviceTexelDenormals
(78ed264c; also from NATIVE_RELAYED), MetalLevelNotMacOS and
MipmapsAsAppleM4 (ec72c052). From HEARD: MetalLevelBelowHost (ec72c052).
From the placement test's relayed lists: ExactFormsOverCompilerLimit
(3c129f4d) and DeviceUnorm8LinearFilter (78ed264c). MipmapsWithinSpread
and MipmapTieRounding were replaced upstream by DeviceFilteredMipmaps
(5d09f454), which takes their place in DIES (dies in strict mode,
relayed by default, not natively relayed, as they were).

New kinds. DeviceAlphaCoverage (524c2f73), DevicePackConversion
(9afdb1e1) and DeviceVertexConversion (96b6f3d1) are notes of the
device's own fixed-function answers, which earlier runtimes gave without
announcing anything. They are placed as relayed precision notes, not in
DIES, so no mode dies of them where none did before. Placement only
matters in strict and census mode: by default only DIES_BY_DEFAULT
(unchanged) dies.

Tests. Linux-compiled tests follow the API: the format_info tests check
the one release's table (264 formats, the setter's values, block and
name reads, wrapped layouts via TextureLevelInfo::of); the
REIMS_VGPU_EXACT test covers the two names, dropped names and "all";
the creator-death test refuses with DeviceLost in place of the removed
HostReleaseUnmeasured; the unmeasured-release test and the
release-comparison test are gone; the resolve test keeps the device
resolve half (ResolvePolicy is gone); depth/stencil and fill tests take
27.0.1's answers. macOS-only metal_tests take 27.0.1's arm where they
matched on the level and drop their checks of the removed mipmap kinds;
their YCbCrFilterPolicy::Exact tests (device/tests/metal_tests.rs,
ycbcr/sampling.rs) are not ported, as that exact filter no longer
exists, and those modules are not compile-checked here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
